# Unit Testing with Google Test

When adding a function or fixing a bug, add corresponding tests in `src/unitTests/<Component>/<Component>_tests.cpp`.

## Test File Structure
```cpp
#include <gtest/gtest.h>
#include "../../path/to/Component.hpp"

using namespace geruest;

class ComponentTest : public ::testing::Test {
protected:
    Component* obj;
    void SetUp()    override { obj = new Component(); }
    void TearDown() override { delete obj; }
};

TEST_F(ComponentTest, DescribesBehavior) {
    EXPECT_EQ(obj->method(), expectedValue);
}
```

## Edge Cases to Always Cover
- **Default/empty state** — fresh object before any setup
- **Boundary values** — min, max, zero, empty string, whitespace-only
- **Invalid input** — wrong types, out-of-range values, malformed data
- **Toggle behaviour** — enable → disable → re-enable sequences
- **Duplicate operations** — adding the same item twice
- **Order independence** — result shouldn't depend on call order when not expected to

## Registering a New Test Executable
If adding tests for a new component, add to `src/unitTests/CMakeLists.txt`:
```cmake
add_executable(MyComponent_Tests MyComponent/MyComponent_tests.cpp ../path/MyComponent.cpp)
target_link_libraries(MyComponent_Tests ${PLATFORM_LIBS} GTest::gtest_main)
gtest_discover_tests(MyComponent_Tests)
```

## Running Tests
```bash
cd src/unitTests/build && ctest --output-on-failure
# Or a single suite:
./build/MyComponent_Tests
```
